{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/35993-merchandise","id":35993,"title":"Merchandise","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-23T18:37:54-08:00","id":35993,"title":"Merchandise","content":"I don't know if this is the right place for this thread, but I had some questions and I hope the staff and any collectors out there can help me.<br /> <br /> Does anyone know where I can find a list, or have created one themselves of all the White-Wolf classic Merchandise that was released?<br /> <br /> I've collected quite a bit myself, but the types of merchandise I have seem rather inconsistent and I'd like to make sure whether I'm on a wild goose chase with certain items that never existed, but it's hard to find any information. I know about a lot of the more popular things like the Tribe necklaces, Clan pins and the famous Werewolf Klaive and the Assamite kukri dagger. But what about the more obscure stuff?<br /> <br /> For example I own a Chessex trademarked Werewolf the Apocalypse coffee mug. I have seen a photo posted on the old forum of their Mage the Ascension mug. Are there other mugs that were created? Vampire? Wraith?<br /> <br /> I'm not asking to buy anything from anyone, I'm just trying to find a list of what all the merchandise is.<br /> <br /> As a side note I managed to find 2 sets of candle holders. One of them is for Vampire and another for Werewolf. The werewolf one is covered in carvings of all the tribe glyphs in pewter. However I noticed something seemed off about the glyphs. I checked a book and discovered that all of the glyphs were Backwards! XD","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T18:56:48-08:00","id":35998,"title":"","content":"There was a Vampire mug with Bradstreet art on it sitting in the lunch room when I started at White Wolf. I think it was Setites, but don't remember for sure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T19:13:48-08:00","id":36008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/35993-merchandise?p=35998#post35998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There was a Vampire mug with Bradstreet art on it sitting in the lunch room when I started at White Wolf. I think it was Setites, but don't remember for sure.</div> </div> </div> </div>Awesome. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I have heard though that staffers got certain merchandise that never got released for mass production due to expense or other issues. Don't suppose you have a photo of the mug?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T22:15:40-08:00","id":36134,"title":"","content":"I have the <i>Vampire</i> mug and chess set (I'm drinking whiskey from the mug as I type this). I used to have the other mugs - and they only did the big 3 - but I gave them away as gifts. I've seen the glasswares - Brujah shot glass, Malkavian hurricane glass, Toreador wine glass and a simple <i>Vampire</i> branded wine glass. There was also all the stationary, which you can still find floating around the internet. Let's see... Zippos (<i>Vampire</i>, Camarilla, Sabbat), flask (<i>Vampire</i>), rings (Camarilla and Sabbat), necklaces... you already mentioned the Clan pins and the Tribe necklaces. It's lte and I don't feel like digging my box out of the office closet, but there's some more. I was more into <i>Vampire</i> when all the merchandise came out, and it was their biggest seller, so that's why there's so much <i>Vampire</i> stuff.<br /> <br /> Cheers!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T22:26:37-08:00","id":36145,"title":"","content":"Nothing: WW put out a Chess set? COOL BEANS! Can you post a photo of it?<br /> <br /> I do have a few zippos and I came across a Convention only merch Vampire Bottle opener. I did not know about the flask, wine glasses or the rings though I guess rings would figure hmm? I did manage to get my hands on a prop blood bag from the Kindred the Embraced series. But I don't think that's quite Merchandise. I vaguely remember the stationary, but it was only for Vampire. I appreciate the help though and if you're rested some time and bored I'd love to know what's in your collection.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-24T10:03:05-08:00","id":36437,"title":"","content":"Off the top of my head (<i>Let me know what I missed</i>).<br /> <br /> <u>For Werewolf/Rage:</u><br /> Rage Baseball cap (<i>I've posted the image of it long ago on LJ, the product comes from White Wolf's Fashion Victim</i>)<br /> Rage T-Shirt<br /> Umbra set Posters (Rage CCG)<br /> W:tA Posters<br /> W:tA T-Shirt (<i>Black with orange logo and orange message on back</i>)<br /> W:tA T-Shirt (<i>I don't own this, but it had a werewolf on it.</i>)<br /> Pentex Polo Shirt<br /> W:tA Mug (<i>I also have this, bought from White Wolf online. It's red with white lighting marks and has the W:tA logo.</i>)<br /> W:tA Candle Holder<br /> W:tA Pin (<i>At least two versions of this</i>)<br /> W:tA Tattoos (<i>Each by Tribe</i>)<br /> W:tA Necklaces (<i>Each by Tribe, each by breed </i><i>except</i><i> for the Ajaba and Bastet Clans</i>)<br /> W:tA Zippo Lighter<br /> W:tA Necklaces, Pins, Earrings made by Java Crypt (<i>Each by Tribe and Wisdom/Glory/Honor</i>)<br /> Rage Plastic Deck Container (<i>Made by Chessex? I remember seeing it once long ago, but I never bought it. It's pinkish red plastic with the Rage logo on it.</i>)<br /> Rage Binder with Umbra Promo (<i>Made by Chessex</i>)<br /> W:tA Book Covers, Regular and Gold (<i>Made by Chessex</i>)<br /> W:tA leather Dicebags (<i>Each by Tribe, saw this on ebay once</i>)<br /> W:tA Dice (<i>Comes with Plastic Tube to put them in.</i>)<br /> W:tA miniatures (<i>Ral Partha</i>)<br /> MET W:tA Gift Deck<br /> W:tWW Poker Deck<br /> Werewolf Klaive<br /> Werewolf Klaive pouch<br /> <br /> <u>Prototypes for things never released:</u><br /> Rage Wars Minaitures<br /> W:tA Action Figures (<i>Al, Mari, and Margrave</i>)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Rage CCG Collector and Artist. Visit the <a href=\"http://rageccg.proboards.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Rage CCG Forums</a>.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img818/5825/w20supportercliath125.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img839/9002/ylxu.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1137,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1137-laughing-hyena","user":"Laughing Hyena","date":". 12-24-2013, 01:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1137-laughing-hyena","name":"Laughing Hyena","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-26T05:24:53-08:00","id":37278,"title":"","content":"Laughing: Wow... that's a lot of merchandise for Werewolf. I have quite a few of those things. The Pentex Polo makes me laugh. I had no idea about those. The Necklaces and Pins from Java's Crypt are the hardest for me to find. (All I want is a GW one darnit!) Don't forget in the necklaces part they also released a sterling silver mini-Klaive pendant. Bought one for my BF, never got it back when we split. I also believe the Werewolf dice were released in tube alone or tube and dice bag. I managed to snag 3 of them from old game friends. The Rage Plastic deck container I remember and found it sort of disappointing. I had no idea that the Klaive replica had a pouch. I've never seen pictures of it, just the custom leather sheath that one proud owner had made for their Klaive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":1332,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","user":"Darling_Rose","date":".  typos! arg! 12-26-2013, 08:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-26T08:43:59-08:00","id":37349,"title":"","content":"Where is thw W:tA flamethrower?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-26T12:20:56-08:00","id":37443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PaladinDemo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/35993-merchandise?p=37349#post37349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where is thw W:tA flamethrower?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure that belongs to hunter the reckoning merchandise. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1700-blue-fox","name":"Blue Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1700_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-09T18:09:52-08:00","id":45957,"title":"","content":"Lets expand this a bit. Anyone have all the dice sets? I've seen pictures of some special Vampire dice with red tips before.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-09T21:37:53-08:00","id":46056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darling_Rose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/35993-merchandise?p=45957#post45957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lets expand this a bit. Anyone have all the dice sets? I've seen pictures of some special Vampire dice with red tips before.</div> </div> </div> </div>There have been WoD themed dice sets that weren't licensed and then there have been chessex dice. I have two - solid black with golden numbers and a rose instead of &quot;1&quot; and dark green with red numbers and an ankh instead of &quot;1&quot;.<br /> Here's a link to chessex: <a href=\"http://www.chessex.com/Dice/Specialty%20Dice/29003.htm\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.chessex.com/Dice/Specialty%20Dice/29003.htm</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To a player who wanted his character to attend a very &quot;special&quot; school:<br /> There is no Charles F. Lupus school for gifted werewolves.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/971-arag","name":"Arag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar971_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-10T05:14:41-08:00","id":46184,"title":"","content":"The original Werewolf dice were produced in Europe. While the numbering and colors were not unique, the combination of colors is something that is not currently in production, which meant that a custom order has to be made to purchase them. Minimum quantities are 2,000 at a time and shipping to the US was in the hundreds of dollars for that 2,000 quantity. That was just for the standard 1-0 numbered dice. Unfortunately, the moon-phase dice were trademarked icons, so I couldn't get those made (plus, it would have been a separate run with custom molds of 2,000 or so of those too) so I didn't have those made <a href=\"http://www.furnation.com/torakhan/werewolfdice/\" target=\"_blank\">when I reproduced the W:tA dice</a>. However, I think that the W:tA dice were the only ones with a custom mold anyways. But others that were custom-colored would still have to be made in larger quantities, packaged, and stored.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">- Arthur &quot;Torakhan&quot; Dreese <span style=\"color:silver\"><b>David &quot;Wall-of-Text&quot; Tealdeer</b> - US2012070036\u200b - Grand Rapids, MI</span><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img855/1250/jv8k.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nmeqe3m\" target=\"_blank\">V:tM 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/pavtnjj\" target=\"_blank\">Hunters Hunted II</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/l3hjgjt\" target=\"_blank\">Anarchs Unbound</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/mxyvsy9\" target=\"_blank\">W:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/k5qe4j4\" target=\"_blank\">W20 Changing Breeds</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/m64m9o5\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3rd Edition</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/qxkop7m\" target=\"_blank\">M:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nd6kms2\" target=\"_blank\">W20BotW</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/780-torakhan","name":"Torakhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar780_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"576"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-10T14:30:38-08:00","id":46502,"title":"","content":"This is one of the weirder ones I've seen, and I somehow ended up with one:<br /> <img src=\"http://bdenmark.members.sonic.net/vampireplate.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\"><b>Demon Cat</b></span><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://flamingporcupine.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Illuminated Dark Ages character sheets and more</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10-demon-cat","name":"Demon Cat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"266"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-11T01:22:31-08:00","id":46789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Torakhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/35993-merchandise?p=46184#post46184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The original Werewolf dice were produced in Europe. While the numbering and colors were not unique, the combination of colors is something that is not currently in production, which meant that a custom order has to be made to purchase them. Minimum quantities are 2,000 at a time and shipping to the US was in the hundreds of dollars for that 2,000 quantity. That was just for the standard 1-0 numbered dice. Unfortunately, the moon-phase dice were trademarked icons, so I couldn't get those made (plus, it would have been a separate run with custom molds of 2,000 or so of those too) so I didn't have those made <a href=\"http://www.furnation.com/torakhan/werewolfdice/\" target=\"_blank\">when I reproduced the W:tA dice</a>. However, I think that the W:tA dice were the only ones with a custom mold anyways. But others that were custom-colored would still have to be made in larger quantities, packaged, and stored.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow, trust Torakhan to come through with the most information, but to shame us all in dedicated fandom. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I wish I had known about your dice sets sooner, I would have totally ordered a bunch. The dice I found are also a pearl copper but they are much too bright. Think New Penny copper. I found them in bulk on Ebay. Copper color, white numbering, but I have painted some silver. Still bright but serviceable for newbies who want werewolf-ish dice and aren't too picky.<br /> <br /> I have noticed something though with the three werewolf sets with Moon dice that I have gotten my paws on. Each one is different in shading. I had an original set that my brother and I shared and it was a sort of yellower brown pearl color. (Will try and take pictures) My brother used to call the werewolf dice Crap dice because to him, they looked like polished turds. I was inclided to agree with him until I managed to win another two sets from someone off of Ebay. Both sets came in original claw marked bag pouches and had the moon dice included, but they were a darker brown pearl color. Almost grayish brown and actually, looked much more turd-like compared to my first set. Over the years I've lost some of my original set and now I can't seem to match it to any other Werewolf dice set. I'll try and post pictures when I can.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-11T01:23:21-08:00","id":46790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demon Cat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/35993-merchandise?p=46502#post46502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is one of the weirder ones I've seen, and I somehow ended up with one:</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That is seriously awesome. I should post a pic of the Blood bag I found. XD","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-11T01:30:10-08:00","id":46792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/35993-merchandise?p=46056#post46056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There have been WoD themed dice sets that weren't licensed and then there have been chessex dice. I have two - solid black with golden numbers and a rose instead of &quot;1&quot; and dark green with red numbers and an ankh instead of &quot;1&quot;.<br /> Here's a link to chessex: <a href=\"http://www.chessex.com/Dice/Specialty%20Dice/29003.htm\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.chessex.com/Dice/Specialty%20Dice/29003.htm</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Those are very interesting, but don't quite resemble the ones I have. I'll have to take some pictures. I have a black set, white numbers, a rose for the 1 and a red tip. I did win a bid for the green speckled red tip set and dice bag in an auction, but it never arrived in the mail. I was very sad. i have not seen a set like that since. I'm surprised they can still be ordered. Though I wish chessex would update their ordering service. This old school email in order is just tedious. Not sure what you mean by dice sets that weren't licensed. I've never seen any that weren't included with an official WW box or stamped tube. I thought the chessex brand were the only company producing WW's dice sets.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T09:47:31-08:00","id":47438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darling_Rose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/35993-merchandise?p=46792#post46792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Those are very interesting, but don't quite resemble the ones I have. I'll have to take some pictures. I have a black set, white numbers, a rose for the 1 and a red tip. I did win a bid for the green speckled red tip set and dice bag in an auction, but it never arrived in the mail. I was very sad. i have not seen a set like that since. I'm surprised they can still be ordered. Though I wish chessex would update their ordering service. This old school email in order is just tedious. Not sure what you mean by dice sets that weren't licensed. I've never seen any that weren't included with an official WW box or stamped tube. I thought the chessex brand were the only company producing WW's dice sets.</div> </div> </div> </div>The dice I had made were pretty darn close (within tollerance for me) of the originals. The new ones were slightly &quot;brighter&quot;, but not by much. This made sense to me because I had them made by the same company that made the originals 20 years ago. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> In doing my research, I saw some dice with white numbers instead of silver. I suspect that the white-numbered dice in the velvet bag may have come out later,<br /> <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/photo.php?fbid=2637376449116\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"https://scontent-a-ord.xx.fbcdn.net/hphotos-ash2/t1/404859_2637376449116_375616329_n.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></a><br /> (Original / New)<br /> <br /> I always bought mine (8 sets, or more, I forget) in the plastic tubes. Over time I've lost all but one tube (and all of the dice, except for three of the numbered dice and two of the moon phase dice.)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/photo.php?fbid=3712315561922\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"https://scontent-b-ord.xx.fbcdn.net/hphotos-ash3/22697_3712315561922_224147798_n.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></a><br /> (Original tube, and the tube filled with the new dice.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">- Arthur &quot;Torakhan&quot; Dreese <span style=\"color:silver\"><b>David &quot;Wall-of-Text&quot; Tealdeer</b> - US2012070036\u200b - Grand Rapids, MI</span><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img855/1250/jv8k.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nmeqe3m\" target=\"_blank\">V:tM 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/pavtnjj\" target=\"_blank\">Hunters Hunted II</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/l3hjgjt\" target=\"_blank\">Anarchs Unbound</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/mxyvsy9\" target=\"_blank\">W:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/k5qe4j4\" target=\"_blank\">W20 Changing Breeds</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/m64m9o5\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3rd Edition</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/qxkop7m\" target=\"_blank\">M:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nd6kms2\" target=\"_blank\">W20BotW</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/780-torakhan","name":"Torakhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar780_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"576"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T16:59:05-08:00","id":47707,"title":"","content":"Torakahn: Very impressive. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> those are really close. Inspired I grabbed my entire box of dice to go through on my work break and discovered some of my sets are missing. Hmm. Specifically the black, red tipped dice I had. And I forgot my werewolf dice are in my ST box, but otherwise I have a collection of about 365 lose dice total. All except 5 dice are in sets of 10. I'll post a photo as soon as I figure out how. Unfortunately I can't upload from my phone, the file size is too big.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T18:30:02-08:00","id":55096,"title":"","content":"If you really want to hunt down a rarity, try to find some of the Wraith Guild-symbol fridge magnets that Henry Higgenbotham sold for a while.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1052-realdeadguy","name":"RealDeadguy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1052_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T20:47:02-08:00","id":55183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RealDeadguy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/35993-merchandise?p=55096#post55096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you really want to hunt down a rarity, try to find some of the Wraith Guild-symbol fridge magnets that Henry Higgenbotham sold for a while.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow! I never knew those existed. I'll have to try and find them. Now many in the set? Were all guilds done? I can't seem to find any photographs of what they look like. Were they resin? or just cardstock on flat magnets with a laminate on top?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-22T02:13:41-08:00","id":55337,"title":"","content":"Some killer stuff in this thread. But I REALLY want to know where I could get my filthy, grubby claws on a Brujah shot glass.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>\u201cAnd those who were seen dancing were thought to be insane by those who could not hear the music.\u201d - Friedrich Nietzsche</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/812-datura","name":"Datura","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar812_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-22T04:52:19-08:00","id":55379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Datura</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/35993-merchandise?p=55337#post55337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some killer stuff in this thread. But I REALLY want to know where I could get my filthy, grubby claws on a Brujah shot glass.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good luck on that one. I keep an eye (and several saved searches) on Ebay for WW merchandise, but I've never come across anyone selling Vampire clan shot glasses. Now that I know they exist you bet I'll leave a fishing line out for them. Best you can do is try the same. Save a search on Ebay and have it email you when someone posts what you're looking for.<br /> <br /> I'm hoping more will come forward with either a list of their personal collection or an official list for the different system merchandise. The Big List of WW books is awesome, and includes novels, comics and even Magazines, but not the Merch. I really hope somewhere out there someone has a list for that stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-22T10:09:05-08:00","id":55534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Datura</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/35993-merchandise?p=55337#post55337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some killer stuff in this thread. But I REALLY want to know where I could get my filthy, grubby claws on a Brujah shot glass.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for reminding me, I meant to come back in this thread and revise that. I hate to break your heart, but after going through my box, it's an Assamite shot glass. Brujah has a beer mug/stein. And Ventrue brandy snifter.<br /> <br /> Cheers!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-22T11:56:31-08:00","id":55593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Datura</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/35993-merchandise?p=55337#post55337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some killer stuff in this thread. But I REALLY want to know where I could get my filthy, grubby claws on a Brujah shot glass.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like this one? From InQuest #35 march 1998, Treasure Chest. These were made by Chessex.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://media.tumblr.com/dbdb879a0e75435996d28015a2b9b05d/tumblr_inline_moek8qrzlY1qz4rgp.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Old photo, but here's the Rage baseball cap I own that was made by White Wolf's Fashion Victim. Still need to take a pic of my Werewolf Mug some day.<br /> <img src=\"http://i9.photobucket.com/albums/a77/Kohryuhyenapet/photos/ragehat.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Rage CCG Collector and Artist. Visit the <a href=\"http://rageccg.proboards.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Rage CCG Forums</a>.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img818/5825/w20supportercliath125.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img839/9002/ylxu.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1137-laughing-hyena","name":"Laughing Hyena","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-22T15:31:21-08:00","id":55743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Laughing Hyena</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/35993-merchandise?p=55593#post55593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like this one? From InQuest #35 march 1998, Treasure Chest. These were made by Chessex.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://media.tumblr.com/dbdb879a0e75435996d28015a2b9b05d/tumblr_inline_moek8qrzlY1qz4rgp.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div> </div> </div> </div>Huh. My Brujah mug might be a knock-off. And the ankh wine-glass doesn't look like the one I have either. But yeah, the brandy snifter is Tremere, not Ventrue. I brain-farted on that one.<br /> <br /> Ah, it's a wine <i>goblet</i>. [ATTACH=CONFIG]n230[/ATTACH]And mine doesn't have the circle of skulls, but the ankh.<br /> <br /> Cheers!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T15:46:06-08:00","id":56396,"title":"","content":"<img src=\"https://31.media.tumblr.com/f5e59554c481aba7a502684eb626c608/tumblr_inline_mzvntkmO391rwmu7n.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <b>White Wolf Publishing 1999 Summer/Fall Catalog</b>:<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Garou Crave Battle</b><br /> Late into the night, your troupe is about to confront the enemy you have struggled to find. He is within your grasp - but you can\u2019t keep your head up. You need coffee!<br /> <br /> <b>Gamers need COFFEE</b><br /> If you\u2019re gonna drink around the gaming table, you might as well do it with class. This Werewolf: The Apocalypse cup is the way to go. It holds a full 12 ounces and is printed on both sides, so you and all your friends can see the logo.<br /> <br /> <b>Stock #:</b> 5301<br /> <b>Retail Price:</b> $12.95 U.S. </div> </div> </div>Same catalog also decribes a Mage: The Ascension Coffee Mug. I'll think that might have been a deep blue or purple glaze.<br /> Way back, I bugged my dad to order this from the White Wolf website back in the day and so far I've never used it (Just keep it in storage). And it's one of the few items I've hardly or never seen on ebay (I've seen what the Werewolf candle votive looks like from ebay).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Rage CCG Collector and Artist. Visit the <a href=\"http://rageccg.proboards.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Rage CCG Forums</a>.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img818/5825/w20supportercliath125.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img839/9002/ylxu.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1137-laughing-hyena","name":"Laughing Hyena","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T17:04:54-08:00","id":56438,"title":"","content":"LH: wow! That's awesome. Much nicer than mine. It's just black with red lettering. It's from Chessex. I'll have to take pics of all my stuff. I do you remember seeing a pic of the mage mug on the old WW forum. I believe it was a dark blue. If there were any purple ones made, there may have been only a few as tests. I managed to score a Vampire Mug off ebay, but no one else bid because it was missing an E at the end of Vampire on one side.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T17:36:45-08:00","id":56462,"title":"","content":"Has anybody tried looking at <a href=\"http://stelio.net/stiki/World_of_Darkness_Products\" target=\"_blank\">Stiki's World of Darkness Products Wiki</a>?<br /> Even then, it's not complete.<br /> I've noticed a few things missing like: Most of the RALV or Rage info (I should have product info thanks to owning this stuff or due to White Wolf Catalogs/CCG Magazines). It doesn't have the two Rage Strategy Guides nor the Rage Calender. Other things are a bit hard to get info as the first few Night Edition Newsletters didn't have White Wolf product codes on them.<br /> <br /> Looking at it: Ah, I knew it. The T-shirt I own isn't the Werewolf: The Apocalypse Revised T-shirt. It's probably the third T-shirt down the line, though. After the 1992 (Tony Harris) and 1995 (Timbrook) one. It's a black T-shirt with logo and writing on the back with three claw marks. The other T-shirts actually had images of a werewolf on them, excluding the Pentex logo Polo shirt.<br /> <br /> <b>Rose:</b> If it was missing an &quot;E&quot;, I don't know why people wouldn't bid on it due that. Misprints often are rarer and much sought after.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Rage CCG Collector and Artist. Visit the <a href=\"http://rageccg.proboards.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Rage CCG Forums</a>.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img818/5825/w20supportercliath125.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img839/9002/ylxu.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1137-laughing-hyena","name":"Laughing Hyena","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T18:32:32-08:00","id":56501,"title":"","content":"I'll have to check that link later on. I'm at work right now, but sounds like it might be kinda useful even if it's missing stuff. The mug was listed as Used even though the description claimed it wasn't. It didn't have an original box. It looks like it might be a misprint. There's no surface damage to indicate it was rubbed off through wear. I'll get pictures of it when I can. Even so I'm fond of my Vampir mug. ^_^","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T19:12:19-08:00","id":56525,"title":"","content":"... oh, that fateful <b>Gangrel jar-mug</b>... I used to carry most of my Werewolf dice in one with a screw-on jar lid... and then lost it... losing both the Gangrel glass AND most of my original Werewolf dice! :.( <br /> <br /> I wish that <a href=\"http://www.javascrypt.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Java's Crypt</a> was still making their jewelry too. I wonder if they still have their molds? Hmm...<br /> <br /> If anyone knows where I can find the <b>Get of Fenris broach</b>, I know someone who's been looking for one for a while and would be quite interested in it...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">- Arthur &quot;Torakhan&quot; Dreese <span style=\"co