se<br /> M:tA Lighter<br /> W:tA Votive Candle and Base<br /> MET Gift Deck<br /> M:tA Votive Candle and Base<br /> Hunter Lighter<br /> MET Discipline Deck 2<br /> V:tM Revised CD-ROM<br /> W:tA Lighter<br /> Werewolf Klaive<br /> Werewolf Scabbard<br /> <br /> <u><b>Quarterly 1.1:</b></u><br /> MET Storyteller Baseball Cap<br /> V:tM Baseball Cap<br /> DA: Werewolf T-shirt<br /> Demon Mousepad<br /> Mage Ether Googles<br /> Exalted T-shirt<br /> DA Revised Dice<br /> Demon Dice<br /> Demon T-shirt<br /> Mage Revised T-shirt<br /> Werewolf Revised T-shirt<br /> <br /> <u><b>Quarterly 1.2:</b></u><br /> Exalted Abyssals T-shirt<br /> <br /> <u><b>Quarterly 1.3:</b></u><br /> Exalted Mousepad<br /> <br /> <u><b>Quarterly 2.1:</b></u><br /> Time of Judgment Clock<br /> Time of Judgment T-shirt<br /> <br /> <u><b>Quarterly 2.2:</b></u><br /> Exalted Essence Beads","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Rage CCG Collector and Artist. Visit the <a href=\"http://rageccg.proboards.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Rage CCG Forums</a>.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img818/5825/w20supportercliath125.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img839/9002/ylxu.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1137,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1137-laughing-hyena","user":"Laughing Hyena","date":". 01-25-2014, 03:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1137-laughing-hyena","name":"Laughing Hyena","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-12T01:27:08-07:00","id":89342,"title":"","content":"@Laughing Hyena, thank you for posting that list! I can't recall seeing that complete of a merchandise list anywhere. It certainly will help me tracking down a few items I need to round out some of my collections.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I'm immortal, I've been right so far&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/301-bwchism","name":"bwchism","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar301_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-12T03:27:42-07:00","id":89375,"title":"","content":"That list brings back memories!<br /> <br /> I still have my Vampire and Werewolf dice. And a stack of cantrip cards somewhere. I sold off my Vampire chess set four or five years ago (I was really disappointed with it). And my Werewolf: The Wild West poker deck last year. I regret not picking up a Klaive though.<br /> <br /> I don't think I see the Diamond Select Vampire: The Masquerade action figures in this thread. They made Lucita, Theo Bell, and Beckett:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.toymania.com/columns/spotlight/dsvampire.shtml\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.toymania.com/columns/spot...svampire.shtml</a><br /> <br /> I still see these in the bargain area of a nearby LCS. They were not very good figures. Although I occasionally entertain the idea of buying Lucita, just for giggles.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/260-chase-variant","name":"Chase Variant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar260_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-12T11:44:20-07:00","id":89616,"title":"","content":"Thanks, bwchism!<br /> <br /> <b>Chase:</b> Diamond Select was also going to make three Werewolf figures, of which (<a href=\"http://www.toymania.com/toyshows/tf2002/full/tf02diamond157.shtml\" target=\"_blank\">Al, Mari, and Margrave</a>) were only ever seen as prototypes at a Toyfair back in 2002. <a href=\"http://www.toymania.com/toyshows/tf2002/full/tf02diamond148.shtml\" target=\"_blank\">Here's an image of them with the vampire figures too.</a> There was also going to be a Werewolf miniatures game under the label &quot;Rage Wars&quot; that never came out too. The guy who sculpted them, Tim Prow, posted them onto cool mini or not:<br /> <a href=\"http://www.coolminiornot.com/19385?browseid=8474674\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery Werewolf</a><br /> <a href=\"http://www.coolminiornot.com/19458?browseid=8474681\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery Bastet</a><br /> <br /> I also recently got a Chessex item that I need to take a picture of: A clear card deck case with the Rage CCG logo painted on. I still need to find the one that I clearly remember seeing way back in 1995/1996 when Comic Books on Parade existed as a store back in Santa Barbara: A red tinted card deck case with the Rage CCG logo engraved into it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Rage CCG Collector and Artist. Visit the <a href=\"http://rageccg.proboards.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Rage CCG Forums</a>.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img818/5825/w20supportercliath125.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img839/9002/ylxu.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1137-laughing-hyena","name":"Laughing Hyena","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-12T17:11:03-07:00","id":89830,"title":"","content":"Would the <a href=\"http://www.nobleknight.com/ViewProducts.asp_Q_ProductLineID_E_751_A_ManufacturerID_E_14_A_CategoryID_E_5_A_GenreID_E_\" target=\"_blank\">Ral Partha miniatures</a> count as merch too?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">- Arthur &quot;Torakhan&quot; Dreese <span style=\"color:silver\"><b>David &quot;Wall-of-Text&quot; Tealdeer</b> - US2012070036\u200b - Grand Rapids, MI</span><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img855/1250/jv8k.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nmeqe3m\" target=\"_blank\">V:tM 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/pavtnjj\" target=\"_blank\">Hunters Hunted II</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/l3hjgjt\" target=\"_blank\">Anarchs Unbound</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/mxyvsy9\" target=\"_blank\">W:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/k5qe4j4\" target=\"_blank\">W20 Changing Breeds</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/m64m9o5\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3rd Edition</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/qxkop7m\" target=\"_blank\">M:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nd6kms2\" target=\"_blank\">W20BotW</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/780-torakhan","name":"Torakhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar780_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"576"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-12T18:21:03-07:00","id":89862,"title":"","content":"And now I'm back. There was a kerfluffle with my computer trying to set up a something I could host pictures on and chat rooms. But my laptop went kaput in the middle of it. <br /> <br /> All better now and I can fix the pictures I tried to post earlier in the thread. And now I've also backed Mage 20th and can have a spiffy backer badge like LH and Torakhan. ^_^. <br /> <br /> Back to Merch. I think the Kindred action figures and Ral Partha minis totally count as Merchandise. In fact I have quite a few of those as well. I think they could have picked better poses for the character minis. Right now a lot of really awesome minis called Lupines are being produced by Reaper Miniatures that captures some of the Shamanism in Werewolf quite well. But it's not technically WW merch. I think of WW's stuff, the minis of the Nexus Crawlers were the best. Unfortunately there were a lot of packaging errors that affected me and other gamers buying NCs. I was so frustrated because it's already a pricy mini but I had to write to the Ral Partha company twice because they sent me a blister that was missing two legs and then had the left side legs doubled. I wound up with 3 Nexus Crawlers though. One with 2 legs and some bent metal legsI made myself, then one with 4 left feet I had to modify to make stand and one complete one. I know of no other mini that gave me so much assembly trouble. They look awesome though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-12T19:50:12-07:00","id":89889,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darling_Rose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/35993-merchandise?p=89862#post89862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was so frustrated because it's already a pricy mini but I had to write to the Ral Partha company twice because they sent me a blister that was missing two legs and then had the left side legs doubled. I wound up with 3 Nexus Crawlers though. One with 2 legs and some bent metal legsI made myself, then one with 4 left feet I had to modify to make stand and one complete one. I know of no other mini that gave me so much assembly trouble. They look awesome though.</div> </div> </div> </div>A Nexus Crawler is something that destroys the fabric of reality around it... so I always thought it was funny that they even had any common visual characteristics. So a Nexus Crawler that was missing, or had multiple &quot;left&quot; legs seems only fitting to me. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">- Arthur &quot;Torakhan&quot; Dreese <span style=\"color:silver\"><b>David &quot;Wall-of-Text&quot; Tealdeer</b> - US2012070036\u200b - Grand Rapids, MI</span><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img855/1250/jv8k.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nmeqe3m\" target=\"_blank\">V:tM 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/pavtnjj\" target=\"_blank\">Hunters Hunted II</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/l3hjgjt\" target=\"_blank\">Anarchs Unbound</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/mxyvsy9\" target=\"_blank\">W:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/k5qe4j4\" target=\"_blank\">W20 Changing Breeds</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/m64m9o5\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3rd Edition</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/qxkop7m\" target=\"_blank\">M:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nd6kms2\" target=\"_blank\">W20BotW</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/780-torakhan","name":"Torakhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar780_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"576"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T19:11:03-07:00","id":106659,"title":"","content":"Finally able to post a pic of my Dice, and yet every time I think I have them all I realize I'm missing something. Ah well. Here it is. It's always growing.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://postimage.org/\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"http://s28.postimg.org/3swqqm14d/Dice.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></a><br /> <a href=\"http://postimage.org/\" target=\"_blank\">image sharing</a><br /> <br /> The dice I own are my attempts at a set for many themes. Several dice were given to me by friends, otherwise I would have only D10s in my collection. the dragon bag on the top has all the non D10s. Next to them are the New WoD dice sets. i would have the Hunter set as well, but I gave that to a friend for Christmas since he enjoys Hunter much more than I do.<br /> <br /> I have 2 different Werewolf bags. The one with the red claw marks was given to me by a friend in Spain and the claw marks seemed to be thermo print rather than paint printed on. He colored them red. The end of one of the marks peeled off, which looking at the other bag I got later on doesn't seem possible with the paint print. The Mage bag has seen better days though the dice it came with were plain purple translucent. I got have some of the purple first run mage dice. They are so very plain looking.<br /> <br /> I forgot about the Glasswalker Leather dice bag I got from someone off of Ebay and forgot about my set of the Time of Judgement dice that are still in the package on my game book shelf. My set of black red-tipped dice are still missing. Nearly all the sets here are complete save for a few random speckled dice and the 5 dice orphans of official WW sets like Mage and Werewolf.<br /> <br /> I debate starting a new thread on just the different dice that WW sold and others that could possibly substitute for CWoD themes discussing all the manufacturers and characteristics of each set, but that might just be something I'm interested in. I do have a question for all out there. Has anyone seen or own a Wraith: the Oblivion dice set with a dice bag? I've only ever found photos of box sets and wraith tubes of dice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":1332,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","user":"Darling_Rose","date":". 04-05-2014, 10:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T19:04:50-08:00","id":432119,"title":"","content":"Bumping this as I've found some swag to ask about and share pics of.<br /> <br /> The first is a Werewolf Candle Holder, (listed as just Werewolf Candle) I also own a Vampire Candle holder that's similar, but can't find it at the moment.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://postimage.org/\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"http://s14.postimg.org/j7c4zvinl/IMG_3735.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></a><br /> <a href=\"http://postimage.org/\" target=\"_blank\">free image host</a><br /> <br /> Now, it's been pointed out in catalog lists that there's a MAGE CANDLE, I'm going to assume is also like this one, however I can't find any pictures anywhere that it's ever existed. Does anyone here own one or have a pic of it? (Also if you look closely at those glyphs you'll notice they look a little off... I don't know who the artist is, but maybe they were having a bad day. Oh well, just one of those things that makes the piece more valuable I guess.<br /> <br /> <br /> And secondly, I've been looking for one of these for ages and finally found a picture. Does anyone own one of these pendants? Can you post pics of it?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://postimage.org/\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"http://s30.postimg.org/nykvok5rl/ww_klaiv.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></a><br /> <a href=\"http://postimage.org/app.php\" target=\"_blank\">take a screenshot</a><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T03:52:22-07:00","id":464496,"title":"","content":"All... all of the glyphs are backwards. *Hyperventilates!*<br /> <br /> That candleholder is neat, I thought it was a drinking glass before I actually read the post (straight to the pictures for instant gratification). May have to go on the hunt now...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><a href=\"http://thecyberrecord.net\" target=\"_blank\">The Cyber Record</a> is on the </span></b><a href=\"http://geomid.network\" target=\"_blank\"><b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">Geomid.Network</span></b></a><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">Activism is Gaian praxis</span></b></div> <div align=\"right\"> <div class=\"img_align_center_wrapper\"><a href=\"https://www.thecyberrecord.net/quests\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" ><img itemprop=\"image\" data-align=\"center\" data-linktype=\"1\" data-linkurl=\"https://www.thecyberrecord.net/quests\" data-size=\"full\" border=\"0\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" data-thumb-url=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment align_center\" /></a></div><br /> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2810-yakecen-sings","name":"Yakecen-Sings","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2810_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T13:10:33-07:00","id":465070,"title":"","content":"Well I don't have much but I do have the following:<br /> <br /> Wraith pin badge<br /> Malkavian pin badge<br /> Music from the Succumbs Club CD (not sure if that counts)<br /> Vampire dice<br /> Gehenna dice<br /> And a Promethian stress brain (yes not cwod but it's a brain!)<br /> I did have a malkavian t shirt but it disintegrated. Luckily I now have redbubble","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>I'm God's hated messenger, the Devil's cohort<br /> I'm the one they all blame, when a life is cut short<br /> But still if you're willing, to give it a try<br /> I'll beat you at anything, and claim you're last sigh</i><br /> - The Reaper's Tales","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4688-malkira","name":"Malkira","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T21:42:48-07:00","id":465634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malkira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/35993-merchandise?p=465070#post465070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well I don't have much but I do have the following:<br /> <br /> Wraith pin badge<br /> Malkavian pin badge<br /> Music from the Succumbs Club CD (not sure if that counts)<br /> Vampire dice<br /> Gehenna dice<br /> And a Promethian stress brain (yes not cwod but it's a brain!)<br /> I did have a malkavian t shirt but it disintegrated. Luckily I now have redbubble</div> </div> </div> </div>Ooo the music from the Succubus Club CD is quite rare indeed. Do you have pics of the stress brain? That would be awesome to see.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-02T03:12:09-07:00","id":465863,"title":"","content":"I have the Mage Tarot. I have no idea how rare it is, but it still makes me quite happy. Also, in my early uni years I wore a custom made Glass Walker pendant. Sadly I lost it to an ex, and I never really wanted to see her enough to push for it to be returned.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T19:00:29-07:00","id":468068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/35993-merchandise